      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "[SCENE START]\n\n**ELEANOR (The Traditionalist)**, standing in her garden, hands a watering can with the water spilling slowly down the sun-warmed stones.\n\"The spring always comes late in these parts, like we did last year, but a solid river cannot be made in a single storm. We have built this valley wall by wall for a century, and you all seem ready to tear it all down to build one big house where everyone can see the same door. I don't want us to fight each other over the timeline of our happiness. Let the voters decide the path in the light of yesterday, but let us tend to the soil we share with our children. The ground does not forgive a landslide.\"\n\n**JAX (The Progressive)\",** pacing the dirt path with hand over the choker, stopping to glare.\n\"Good Lord, no! You're talking about a garden while the real estate market is a scorched field! They ignored the promises in the polls and sold us lives anyway. You think the people will wait for 'the next time' to address the housing crisis, the debt, the smoke in the air? We are the first to see the first and we must take the",
